# Committed acceptance data is written back by the bench harness
# (`python -m bench.framework.cli build | selfcheck`), which emits LF. Under
# `core.autocrlf=true` a Windows checkout materializes these as CRLF, so
# running the documented verification command dirtied all 576 task manifests
# with line-ending-only diffs. Pinning them to LF makes the checkout and the
# writer agree, so `git status` after a bench run reports what actually
# changed.
bench/tasks/**/*.json text eol=lf
bench/reports/*.json text eol=lf
